{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-PostHog","title":"Sending to PostHog"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"role":"collection","title":"PostHogEncoding","externalID":"PostHogEncoding","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s "},{"code":"\/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the like).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more than "},{"code":"Int64.max","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" milliseconds from 1970), and one too large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for PostHog’s event limit. The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use "},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogBatchEncoder":{"type":"topic","title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogEncodingError":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PostHogEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s requests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no record of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogencodingerror"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"title":"postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/posthog(projecttoken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"postHog","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"projectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"host","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<",